{"toolCallId":"call_dfecc89e2c8d4f27835e12948ae4e136","status":"completed","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"text","text":"3:description: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>\"\n26:**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n44:- [ ] T001 Record the current report and exit status for the fixture folder (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S $F; echo \"exit=$?\"` prints the report and `exit=0`.\n45:- [ ] T002 Read the option loop and the trailing `exit 0` (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n 'exit 0|--file\\|-f' $S` prints the parser case and the final `exit 0`.\n53:- [ ] T003 Add a `MIN_PERCENT` global beside `SINGLE_FILE`, empty by default (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n '^MIN_PERCENT=' $S` prints one line.\n54:- [ ] T004 Parse `--min-percent <N>` in the option loop and reject a missing value with exit 1 (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --min-percent` prints `ERROR:` on stderr and `echo \"exit=$?\"` prints `exit=1`.\n55:- [ ] T005 Reject a non-integer or out-of-range N with exit 1 and an `ERROR:` line on stderr (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --min-percent 101 $F` prints `ERROR:` on stderr and `echo \"exit=$?\"` prints `exit=1`.\n56:- [ ] T006 Compare the printed percentage with N after the output call and exit 3 when it is below (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --min-percent $((P+1)) $F; echo \"exit=$?\"` prints `exit=3`.\n57:- [ ] T007 Add the option to the `show_help()` block (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --help | rg -- '--min-percent <N>'` prints one line.\n58:- [ ] T008 Record exit code 3 in the trailing exit-code comment (`$S`). Verify: `rg -n '^#   3' $S` prints one line.\n66:- [ ] T009 Prove the report is unchanged with the option present (`$S`). Verify: `diff <(bash $S $F) <(bash $S --min-percent 0 $F)` prints nothing.\n67:- [ ] T010 Prove both threshold outcomes against the same run (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --min-percent $P $F; echo \"exit=$?\"` prints `exit=0`, and `bash $S --min-percent $((P+1)) $F; echo \"exit=$?\"` prints `exit=3`.\n68:- [ ] T011 Prove `--file` mode applies the floor to the file's own completion (`$S`). Verify: `bash $S --file $F/spec.md --min-percent 100; echo \"exit=$?\"` prints `exit=0` for a file with no placeholders.\n69:- [ ] T012 Re-run strict validation on this packet (`specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent`). Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent --strict | tail -1` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"69f161","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
